Z||000000||beachbomb||06-02-2001||09:34 AM||||Hi, i just pulled my left rear strut out to replace it and i can't get the top nut off of the strut to let the spring out, any ideas! Should i have losened this nut prior to removing the strut??...Help..Jim(2 '84 INdys)||||reg||5
Z||000001||TRiAD||06-02-2001||09:43 AM||||Compress the spring. <BR>Try WD-40 or other penetrating lubricant, and LOTS of tourque. <P>Hope that helps!<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Looking for a white '88 GT 5 sp...<BR>...Could it be...Found?<BR>Stay tuned!</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||06-02-2001||10:18 AM||||Nut splitter time.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||06-02-2001||11:52 AM||||Use vice grips to hold the shaft from spinning when you turn the nut.<BR>Get some thing to keep the spring from shooting the spring cap through the roof. I dont remember how much pressure is on the cap but just be carefull  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/sig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-02-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||06-02-2001||12:02 PM||||I compress the spring and then use an impact on them.||||reg||1
Z||000005||beachbomb||06-02-2001||06:11 PM||||Hi all, just completed the job, thanks for your advice, i had the springs compressed, finally found my mechanic and used his air tools and finally got them off, thanks again..jim||||reg||10
